{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2526","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2526","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2526\",\"parent_revision\":\"aeeb90e1a4c7332811fb5dcdda625d8dae8ee4f684fc4c6d8e274be8d752d73c\",\"root_revision\":\"aeeb90e1a4c7332811fb5dcdda625d8dae8ee4f684fc4c6d8e274be8d752d73c\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nMarkdownIndexer.build() in progressive_markdown/indexer.py is a 150-line token-walk monolith with 74 statements and 40 local variables, both well above ruff's thresholds (PLR0915: >50 statements, PLR0914: >15 locals). The method mixes three concerns: (1) token stream dispatch, (2) section graph construction, and (3) code block extraction. Decompose into private helpers: _process_heading_token(), _process_fence_token(), _finalise_sections(), and a _BuildState dataclass to carry local state across helpers. Each piece should be independently testable.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-06-03)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: No other backlog items are blocked on this specific item.\\n- Bottleneck: Until verified, a developer maintaining `indexer.py` cannot tell from the issue whether the work is complete. The missing test-run confirmation is the only gap.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `MarkdownIndexer.build()` is no longer a PLR0915/PLR0914 violation; ruff CI passes cleanly.\\n- Each extracted helper (`_process_heading_token`, `_process_fence_token`, `_finalize_sections`) is independently testable.\\n- `_BuildState` dataclass replaces 40 local variables with a named, typed accumulator.\\n- The characterisation test suite pins the behavioral contract against regression.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter the refactor (already in place), `MarkdownIndexer.build()` delegates to three private helpers via `_process_tokens()` and `_finalize_sections()`. The returned `MarkdownDocument` is structurally and field-value identical to what the monolithic version produced on the same `ParserResult`. Running `ruff check --select PLR0915,PLR0914 progressive_markdown/indexer.py` exits 0.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe target state already exists in the codebase:\\n\\n- `indexer.py` \u2014 `MarkdownIndexer` class with four focused methods; `_BuildState` and `_SectionBuilder` dataclasses at module level; module-level helpers `_make_slug`, `_build_selector`, `_code_summary`.\\n- `test_indexer_decomposition.py` \u2014 PLR lint-gate test class + five behavioral characterisation test classes covering all heading/code/span contract requirements.\\n\\nThe file should be closed once test execution confirms both gate and behavioral tests pass.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `ruff check --select PLR0915,PLR0914` on `indexer.py` exits 0.\\n2. `pytest test_indexer_decomposition.py` exits 0; `TestPLRLintGate.test_indexer_build_passes_plr_complexity_gates` passes GREEN.\\n3. `build()` is a short orchestrator delegating to `_process_tokens()` and `_finalize_sections()` \u2014 already satisfied (13 lines in current file).\\n4. `_BuildState` dataclass carries all cross-helper mutable state \u2014 already satisfied.\\n5. Three helpers (`_process_heading_token`, `_process_fence_token`, `_finalize_sections`) are distinct named methods \u2014 already satisfied.\\n6. Public interface `MarkdownIndexer().build(result)` is unchanged \u2014 already satisfied.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/indexer.py` \u2014 refactored source file |\\n| Prior work | `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/test_indexer_decomposition.py` \u2014 PLR gate + behavioral characterisation tests |\\n| Backlog | #2498 \u2014 decompose `backlog_core` operations.py/server.py (related decomposition pattern, different scope) |\\n| Backlog | #1048 \u2014 Fix PLR0914 in `session_audit.py` (same lint rule family, independent scope) |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 refactor is self-contained within `progressive_markdown/indexer.py`.\\n- Blocks: None identified.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the implementation is already in place. Remaining work is running `ruff check` and `pytest` to confirm the item is DONE, then closing the issue.\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Refactor\\n- Behavioral boundary: The public interface of `MarkdownIndexer.build()` \u2014 it receives a `ParserResult` and returns a `MarkdownDocument` with identical field values before and after decomposition. No new observable behavior is introduced; existing behavior is preserved.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Acceptance criteria must prove (a) the PLR violations no longer exist in `indexer.py`, and (b) the behavioral contract of `build()` is identical to pre-refactor output on the same inputs.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- Test execution confirmation is outstanding. The refactor appears complete from static inspection of `indexer.py` but `pytest` and `ruff check` have not been run in this grooming session to confirm the PLR lint-gate test passes.\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\nFiles directly changed by this refactor:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/indexer.py` \u2014 the only file modified; all changes are internal (private methods, internal dataclasses)\\n\\nFiles with verified behavioral contract (read-only, not modified):\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/models.py` \u2014 `MarkdownDocument`, `SectionNode`, `CodeBlock`, `SourceSpan` models; public API unchanged\\n- `plugins/development-harness/progressive_markdown/parser.py` \u2014 `ParserResult`; unchanged\\n\\nTest files that gate this item:\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/tests/unit/progressive_markdown/test_indexer_decomposition.py`\\n\\nCallers of `MarkdownIndexer` in the wider codebase: any code calling `MarkdownIndexer().build(result)` is unaffected because the public method signature is unchanged.\\n\\n### Implementation Status\\n\\n**The refactor described in this item has already been applied.**\\n\\nAs of grooming date 2026-06-03, `progressive_markdown/indexer.py` contains:\\n\\n- `_SectionBuilder` dataclass (lines 33-48) \u2014 mutable accumulator per section\\n- `_BuildState` dataclass (lines 51-63) \u2014 carries all mutable state across helper calls\\n- `MarkdownIndexer.build()` \u2014 13-line orchestrator delegating to helpers\\n- `MarkdownIndexer._process_tokens()` \u2014 dispatches to heading/fence handlers\\n- `MarkdownIndexer._process_heading_token()` \u2014 heading concern isolated\\n- `MarkdownIndexer._process_fence_token()` \u2014 code block extraction concern isolated\\n- `MarkdownIndexer._finalize_sections()` \u2014 section graph construction concern isolated\\n\\nTest file `test_indexer_decomposition.py` encodes the pre/post gate:\\n\\n- `TestPLRLintGate` \u2014 runs `ruff check --select PLR0915,PLR0914`; RED before, GREEN after refactor\\n- Five behavioral characterisation classes \u2014 pin the `build()` output contract; GREEN before and after\\n\\n**Outstanding**: Run `ruff check` and `pytest` to confirm GREEN. Item is then ready to close.\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Decompose `MarkdownIndexer.build()` into private helpers and a `_BuildState` dataclass so each concern is independently testable and ruff PLR0915/PLR0914 violations are eliminated.\\n- Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Source file `progressive_markdown/indexer.py` is readable and analysable.\\n  - Ruff rule codes PLR0915 (too many statements) and PLR0914 (too many local variables) are standard with known thresholds (50 statements, 15 locals).\\n  - Existing test file `test_indexer_decomposition.py` provides a pre-written RED/GREEN gate for the PLR rules and a full characterisation suite for behavioral equivalence.\\n  - The decomposition has already been applied: `_process_heading_token()`, `_process_fence_token()`, `_finalize_sections()`, and `_BuildState` are all present in the file.\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Whether the PLR lint-gate test passes can be verified by running `ruff check --select PLR0915,PLR0914` against `indexer.py`. The test harness already encodes this check.\\n  - Whether the behavioral tests remain GREEN can be verified by running `pytest` on `test_indexer_decomposition.py`.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - Confirmation that `TestPLRLintGate.test_indexer_build_passes_plr_complexity_gates` currently passes. The refactor appears complete from inspection, but test execution has not been confirmed in this grooming session.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **refactor: decompose markdownindexer.build() monolith \u2014 150 lines, plr0915/plr0914** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Code review of progressive_markdown package \u2014 2026-05-31, surfaced by implementing agent during indexer off-by-one investigation\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-06-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"6bb500f06a9f39257b6a0b6ec9805e696fa8ef1e0f7dbc21538d902da9b662f4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTA4QQ\"}"}